			"Sections": [
                {
                  "SectionId": "difficulty",
                    "SectionName": "Difficulty Settings",
					"SectionDescription": "Monster Tiers:\nTier 0 (Zero): The weakest monsters. Rats, spiderlings, weakened Imps.\nTier 1 (Low): Basic monsters from Act 1\nTier 2 (Mid): Level 2-4 Classed NPCs, monsters have tricks\nTier 3 (High): Midgame monsters, specialized NPCs like Anders\nTier 4 (Ultra): Advanced monsters like Gish'ra, Earlygame bosses\nTier 5 (Epic): Advanced NPCs and Midgame bosses\nTier 6 (Legendary): Endgame boss NPCs and exceptionally powerful monsters.\nTier 7 (Mythical): Ansur, Netherbrain, and beings comparable to the strongest in the vanilla game\nTier 8 (Divine): Demigods, Tarrasque, creatures adapted from tabletop D&D5e beyond the experience of vanilla BG3\nTier 9 (Avatar): Challenge Rating 30 avatars of true deities, the upper ceiling of D&D5e material.\n\nBoosts are added to the original Tier value of the mob, i.e. a Tier 2 NPC who gets Boost 2 will be treated as a Tier 4 NPC when randomized.\nIf set with a Randomization Ceiling of 1 and a Randomization Floor of 0, this example NPC could be randomized into either a Tier 4 or Tier 5 enemy.",
                    "Settings": [
						{
                            "Id": "preset_normal",
                            "Name": "Preset Difficulty: Normal",
                            "Description": "Randomized enemies will be closely bounded to the difficulty of their original counterparts.",
                            "Type": "checkbox",
